================================================================================
SCOPE OF THE MIT LICENSE ABOVE, AND TERMS FOR MATERIAL IT DOES NOT COVER
================================================================================

The MIT licence above applies to the original work in this repository: the
source code under src/, scripts/, app/, and tests/, the configuration files
under configs/, and the written documentation (README.md, DATASET.md,
PLANNING.md, and docs/).

It does NOT apply to the two items below.

1. THE DATASET — not distributed here
-------------------------------------
The PV Panel Defect Dataset is licensed by its uploader under
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
(CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), which permits NON-COMMERCIAL use only.

    https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/alicjalena/pv-panel-defect-dataset
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

No dataset image is included in this repository; data/ is gitignored apart
from image-free metadata (manifests, hashes, split definitions, and audit
tables). Anyone reproducing this work must obtain the dataset themselves under
its own terms — see DATASET.md.

As stated in DATASET.md, this is a community-uploaded aggregation of images
from multiple public web sources. The uploader's licence reflects their right
to license the compilation; it does not by itself establish that every
underlying photograph's original rights-holder consented to that
redistribution. No image is claimed as original work by this project.

2. THE TRAINED MODEL WEIGHTS — models/solarguard_baseline_v1.pt
---------------------------------------------------------------
These weights were produced by training on the dataset described above, and
are therefore treated as a derivative of CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 material. They are
made available under the SAME terms as that dataset — CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 —
and NOT under the MIT licence:

  - NonCommercial: no commercial use.
  - ShareAlike: distribute any adaptation under these same terms.
  - Attribution: credit this project and the original dataset.

This is the conservative reading, chosen deliberately rather than asserting
that the weights are unencumbered. It matches the statement in
docs/MODEL_CARD.md that downstream use of the trained weights inherits the
non-commercial restriction.

The code that produced the weights remains MIT-licensed; retraining it on data
you have your own rights to yields weights this restriction does not touch.
